nalPhonemes","fan","fast","jam","lump","milk","near — above does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","oa changes the required spelling of the exact dictated word.","plum","sharedLexicalSet","slug","up","vest","watermelon","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/mud-63ab413311.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/pot-219afba4c6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/red-423dcd39be.mp3","Retain and order at least four phonemes, including an initial or final consonant cluster, rather than the three-phoneme entry sequence.","The first complete sentence is “Ice covered the puddle.”","The first complete sentence is “The gardener brought water.”","The first complete sentence is “The ice began to melt.”","The first complete sentence is “The phone rang.”","The first complete sentence is “The towel lay in a puddle.”","The first complete sentence is “Two pictures covered the table.”","Two occurrences must each be associated with its own contextual sense.","Use both occurrences to match two distinct senses, with two unused meanings.","car","context_clues","down","feed","happy","horse","hot","laugh","look","meaning_at_named_occurrence","orderedSenses","otherSense","pet","queriedOccurrence","queriedSense","requiredAssignments","sheep","shut","simple","smell","sofa","spareMeanings","targetOccurrences","use1","use2","/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/choose-the-two-words-that-mean-more-than-one-aa40fb62c4.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bench-a2d56e8999.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bounce-31e0c28995.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bowl-317e476e69.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/eat-1abfae0063.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/empty-ec61baf9de.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/give-useful-guidance-while-leaving-another-person-a-chance-to-try-9ac008321a.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/long-07c39be44d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/mat-faaaac327f.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/quick-0d94c80d53.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/ride-bfdbf56047.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/run-03dad31a03.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/scarf-0f8b1139c7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/shake-a166e3d7ad.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/short-c830ea4a1d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/shout-2084ada19d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/sneeze-20840024be.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/spin-495df0f115.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/stand-0ab77d421c.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-the-same-conditions-when-making-a-fair-comparison-fdf0c17e88.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/wide-06aafe8dc2.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/write-e08ef6e83a.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/mock-v11/433af56b78bda8ea92.mp3","/images/assessment/blends/broom.webp","/images/assessment/blends/drum.webp","/images/assessment/digraphs/phone.webp","/images/assessment/digraphs/sock.webp","/images/assessment/generated/initial-sounds-l2/camera.webp","/images/assessment/generated/sequencing/child-drinks-water.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/ball-below-shelf.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/dog-next-to-bench.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/light-above-table.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-chin.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-dress.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-horse.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/object-atlas-v1.webp#mock-cell=4","/images/assessment/objective-words/lion.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/net.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/pan.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/snake.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/tiger.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/tooth.webp","/images/assessment/release-support/targets/ball-8bec04.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/ar/star-02.webp","/images/child-mode/blends/slide.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/bear.webp","/images/child-mode/vocabulary/hair.webp","/images/child-mode/vocabulary/soup.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/pillow.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/scarf.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/towel.webp","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly.","Allow a change to finish before the next step.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work.","Check identity instead of relying on a quick resemblance.","Check unclear directions before choosing what to do.","Check what another person can actually see.","Check what is true before acting on a guess.","Choose a manageable part and share work that is too much.","Choose a tool that fits the particular job.","Choose by the job a thing must do, not its looks.","Choose the two words that mean more than one.","Compare finished work with its guide before moving on.","Decoration should leave the useful parts able to work.","Distinguish a familiar object from closely related concrete pictures.","Do needed earlier steps before starting later ones.","Explain unfamiliar routines so a newcomer can take part.","Explain your own mistake so it can be put right.","Find out what someone needs before making a choice.","Find the cause instead of repeating a temporary fix.","Find the first event in a chronological account.","Gardeners choose plants for a new garden.","HOMOPHONE_ERROR_LOCATION_V4","Help repair the damage when something goes wrong.","How returned books are checked in and sorted.","How to fix a broken classroom toy.","How to pick seeds for a new flower bed.","Leave enough space for things to work properly.","Locate one misused homophone while retaining another correct occurrence of exactly the same printed word. Its meaning and grammatical role, rather than spotting the spelling, determine which token needs changing.","Look for evidence before deciding what a problem means.","Make room for what is needed before adding extras.","One successful check does not check every part.","Plan how to carry out a job you have promised.","Record the arrangement before taking something apart.","Search in an order that avoids checking places repeatedly.","Take care of useful supplies that other people share.","Tell affected people when a plan changes.","The first complete sentence is “Although the clock stopped, the class kept working.”","The first complete sentence is “Before the soup cooled, the cook stirred it.”","The first complete sentence is “The puppy curled up.”","The first complete sentence is “The string snapped.”","The printed sentence supplies the contextual spelling evidence. Only the exact error-location direction is narrated; no token or replacement is spoken as an answer clue.","Try a small test before doing the whole job.","Use enough containers for the amount you have.","Use the amount needed instead of adding the most.","Use the same starting reference when comparing results.","Useful instructions need all the important details.","When a method fails, try a different approach.","bear","begin — wait","bet","bud","build","correctHomophoneTokenIndex","correctlyUsedSameSpellingOccurrences","cub","dog","errorTokenIndex","gas","homophonePair","homophones","hum","list","lp3.homophones_homonyms.l1.A.sea_see.v1","mock.relations.opposite-quality","mouth","muddy","needs","original_mock_v4_word_ladder","pat","quiet","replacement","requiresOccurrenceContext","rib","sameSpellingOccurrences","src/data/literacyMockWordLaddersV4.js","text_only","wait","wordCount",36,37,"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/ball-575efc20cc.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bike-21fb12d912.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/blanket-30f4aed2c9.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/broom-054dd95416.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/brush-a56761a2d7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bus-f9f7984558.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/coat-65e8377bf7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/dig-41ebf00471.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/hop-02f63976ff.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/map-1febcbc483.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/mop-e235065535.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/sat-9f3e1919d7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/star-160c94f740.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/tent-bd9a8151e4.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/top-de7980f068.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/sun-986667ed8b.mp3","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-cut.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/sofa.webp","Ada hung the picture list above her own head. The younger children could not see what to collect. She crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it.","Alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. The paint dried while she searched. Before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint.","Amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. Its owner came looking for it. Amir checked the name inside and returned it. Then he checked another blue coat and found his own name.","Asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. Her friend kept waiting under the tree. Asha went back and explained the change. Her friend brought his bag to the dry porch.","Bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. The base bent under the model. She tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base.","Bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. He put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. Bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office.","Eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. He practiced its first short part, then the next part. After joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through.","Ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. A different wheel stuck when he pushed it. He turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again.","Finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. The wet joint slid apart. He glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. This time the handle stayed on.","Grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. The book was too wide. She asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it.","I","Imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. The paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. She cut the paper away from the moving wheel. The cart rolled again.","Jo kept the game scores in her head. After a break she could not remember which team had seven points. On the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. The teams could check the score after the break.","Kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. Beads bounced onto the floor. He held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. The beads went into the bottle.","Luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. They spilled whenever he moved it. He divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. He carried both trays without losing beans.","Maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. The puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. She replaced the tray. After the next watering, the shelf stayed dry.","Mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. When the flags dried, the paint cracked. She tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again.","Noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. Then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. For the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon.","Olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. The copied pattern was different. Olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. Her friend used it to rebuild the pattern.","Omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. When the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. For his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead.","Poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. She chose the wrong longer strip. She laid them flat with their left ends together. Now she could see which strip reached farther.","Quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. It soaked through and wrinkled the paper. On the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. The card stayed flat.","Ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. A gust blew two pages across the yard. He moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. The pages stayed where he put them.","Ren took every shelf out of a toy cupboard to clean it. Later she could not tell which shelf had fitted each space. Before cleaning the next cupboard, she put matching marks on the shelves and their spaces. They went back easily.","Represent each of the 4 phonemes of the dictated word with its ordered grapheme.","Sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. His cousin arrived on the wrong morning. Sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic.","Suri copied a striped flag and thought it was finished. When she held it beside the original, she noticed a missing white stripe. She added it, then compared the two flags once more.","Tariq kept searching the same three drawers for a missing stamp. He could not remember which ones he had checked. He placed an empty card beside each searched drawer and moved to the next one. He found the stamp in a new drawer.","Tess pushed all her seedlings into one corner of the tray. Their leaves overlapped and bent. She moved them farther apart into the empty spaces. The leaves no longer pressed against one another.","The exact word is dictated. Only silent printed letter/grapheme tiles are offered; pictures and spoken tile labels cannot give away its spelling.","The first complete sentence is “Because the basket fell, the apples rolled.”","The first complete sentence is “Because the boat rocked, the sailor sat down.”","The first complete sentence is “Rain soaked the tent.”","The first complete sentence is “The players gathered by the goal.”","Zara pushed the same puzzle piece harder each time it would not fit. The cardboard began to bend. She stopped pushing, turned the piece, and found the position that matched the gap.","awake","basket","best","comb","crab","egg","end","floats","fun","in","mock.relations.same-precise","open","our","pop","rabbit","responseTiles","responseUnitCount","rob","sip","skip","skirt","sleep","start","sum","test","tired","tomato","twice","/audio/production/en-US/assessment_prompt/which-word-rhymes-with-the-word-you-hear-598c21a60c.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/cot-a9c2df5a01.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/jet-4231ddc063.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/kit-c72c9565e4.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/man-73c2d6b358.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/mug-056f8accc6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/nut-ab2036ae8f.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/peg-a75e7186e6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/slide-aa19979026.mp3","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-milk.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-swim.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/run.webp","3","Order words or 