tween different flowering plants.","Bees collect nectar to take to their hive.","How a board lists classes that have spare places.","How a class finds warmer days on Friday.","How a class records the sky each morning.","How a closed gate keeps footballs from young plants.","How a helper repairs clothes before the next show.","How a helper replaces worn strings after instruments return.","How a helper reports when a walker needs to stop.","How a high tap leaves room for a bottle.","How a repair sheet tells a team about faults.","How a roof keeps the waiting seats dry.","How a timetable shows the rooms for existing classes.","How a tray drains water instead of letting it collect.","How a worker tests swings before the playground opens.","How an order list helps a helper find missing supplies.","How bright arrows show the route to the car park.","How desk staff explain a change of platform.","How labelled trolleys take books to their shelves.","How measuring ingredients prepares bowls before cooking.","How named rails help actors find their own costumes.","How scanning a returned book clears its loan.","How separate spaces stop apples squashing softer food.","How separate trays help builders choose clean materials.","How shoulder straps spread the weight of a backpack.","How signs above stairs show the platform numbers.","How small pockets keep pencils away from books.","How the office checks descriptions before returning objects.","How the office labels where objects were found.","How the teacher records names beside borrowed instruments.","How two clips hold a lunchbox lid shut.","How volunteers collect books that families have finished.","How volunteers help visitors find books they may enjoy.","How washing tools leaves the kitchen ready afterwards.","How wide paths let visitors walk beside garden beds.","Moving a toy nearer makes larger shadows.","Moving the torch sideways shifts the shadow.","Oiled outer feathers help swimming ducks stay dry.","Picture choices for this literacy question","Printed case is the evidence. The choices have identical wording and punctuation; speaking them or adding an object picture would not establish capitalization.","Represent each of the 3 phonemes of the dictated word with its ordered grapheme.","Retain four spoken phonemes while placing five letters around a split vowel and rejecting two spare letters.","Roots collect water from the surrounding soil.","Roots hold plants firmly in the ground.","Soft inner feathers keep swimming ducks warm.","Start the sentence with one capital letter. These other words use small letters.","The exact printed order and authored line break supply the evidence; the instruction never narrates the answer.","The first complete sentence is “The oven beeped.”","The first complete sentence is “The wind grew stronger.”","The sentence starts with a capital; names and I keep their capitals, while ordinary nouns inside the sentence do not take extra capitals.","They","Track print from the end of one line back to the left edge of the following line.","Use specific feedback to improve unclear work.","We","Which word has the same starting sound?","Which word names an animal?","Worm tunnels let air enter the soil.","Worms pull fallen leaves beneath the ground.","all_none","answer-cards","baker","bank","beach","before","boot","bright","bun","cat behind sofa","checking the address","checking the score","child between trees","clipping up the plan","closing a basket","colouring the picture","damp","dark","dog in front of house","drawing a line","fixing","flag","folding the blanket","folding the map","got","gum","ham","hanging his coat","kept","lifting her basket","listen","melt","messy","mock.relations.same-everyday","mouse","new","nod","not-applicable-scoring-options","opening the packet","original_literacy_guide_v12_beginner_writing","original_mock_depth","paste","picking a flower","pizza","putting down the bag","putting on a coat","reading the sign","ringing the buzzer","rollin