er. The book returned to the shelf.","Bea could not lift the large box and thought she could not help. She carried the loose lids while two others carried the box. The whole set reached the hall together.","Compare a vowel plus one final consonant (or an open spoken rime). A long vowel, spelling digraph, doubled letter or onset cluster is not an extra coda phoneme.","Compare the vowel and ending together to find a spoken rhyme.","D-CONTEXT: I is correctly used at token 1; it is not the homophone error required by this sentence.","D-ONSET","Eli refused to move scenery because he had never done it. At rehearsal he tried moving one light panel with a partner. He liked helping the scene change and chose that job for the play.","Hana left a tap dripping after filling a bowl. A helper showed her the growing puddle in the sink. Hana closed the tap fully, and the dripping stopped.","Ivo scattered the score cards and said the wind had done it. His friend began looking for a loose window. Ivo explained what had happened, and they put the cards back in order.","Jem started down the slide before the child below had moved away. They nearly bumped. Jem waited for the bottom to clear on his next turn, and both children had room.","Lea took a ruler from Ben’s desk because he was outside. Ben returned and could not finish his chart. Next time Lea asked first, and Ben found a spare ruler for her.","Leila said a plant needed water because its leaves hung down. Dad asked her to touch the soil. It was already wet. They moved the pot out of the hot sun instead, and the leaves lifted later.","Mara thought the plain paper bag was empty and nearly recycled it. She looked inside and found the missing puppet shoes. She put the shoes with the puppet before recycling the empty bag.","Milo took over his sister’s puzzle whenever she paused. She had no chance to try a piece. He showed how to find an edge, then handed the pieces back and waited while she tried.","Noor promised to feed the class fish but joined a game and forgot. The teacher fed them. The next day Noor did the feeding job before joining the game and marked it on the chart.","Oli took the whole sheet of gold stickers for his crown. His group had none left. He returned the sheet, and they divided the stickers before finishing everyone’s crowns.","Ren tried carrying a heavy crate alone and could not lift it clear of the floor. He asked a helper to carry the other end. Together they moved it onto the trolley.","The first complete sentence is “Our team arrived.”","The first complete sentence is “The basket fell.”","The first complete sentence is “The dog ran.”","The first complete sentence is “The rain fell.”","The first complete sentence is “The rain stopped.”","The first complete sentence is “The sun rose.”","The group began a game without explaining it to a new child. She ran to the wrong end and stopped. They showed her the goal and played a slow round together before starting again.","The group decorated a cart while its loose wheel still wobbled. The cart could not carry their bags. They fixed the wheel first on the next cart, then added ribbons when it rolled properly.","The printed passage gives the answer “here”.","The shape of b belongs to another letter.","The shape of d belongs to another letter.","The shape of h belongs to another letter.","The shape of l belongs to another letter.","The shape of n belongs to another letter.","Tom told a visitor that the hall was “over there.” The visitor chose the wrong door. Tom named the blue door beside the stairs, and the visitor found the hall.","Two builders pulled their cardboard bridge towards different tables. A joint came loose. They stopped, chose one place together and carried the bridge there side by side.","Two runners began from different lines. The nearer runner won, but nobody knew who was faster. They started again from one line and could compare their running.","Una coloured the blank part of her friend’s drawing to help. Her friend had wanted to leave it white for snow. On the next drawing Una asked what was needed and held the paper instead.","When Kim lost, she pushed the board and scattered the pieces. Her friend stopped playing. Kim helped set it up again and asked for another game without changing the old result.","a clear material for windows","a closure that keeps a lid shut","a container for a drink","a cover that closes a bottle","a curled piece of metal","a dog’s short loud sound","a greeting made with a hand","a kind of music","a large bus for passengers","a metal fastener for wood","a person who trains a team","a piece of material covering a hole","a place that keeps money","a rolling rise of water","a small area of ground","a soft covering for the head","a solid stone material","a storage box with a lid","a tree’s outer covering","a written message sent to someone","an animal that swims in the sea","awake — asleep does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","aʊ","balloon between kites","big does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","book on shelf","boots","bright — quiet does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","child inside bus","child picks apple","child plants seed","child puts on winter hat","child rubbing soap on both hands","child waters seed","children plant tree","chilly","closed","compare_rimes","dirty","empty — light does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","far","first","flower in front of fence","fresh","glove","grass","image+print","kitten in basket","little — small does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","log names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","mock.v11.everyday.listening.0.chin","mock.v11.everyday.listening.0.kangaroo","mock.v11.everyday.listening.0.rain","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.bath","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.bread","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.broom","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.brush","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.butterfly","mock.v11.everyday.liste