duction/en-US/supplemental/hum-7a80133aa6.mp3","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-band.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-camp.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-drop.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-flap.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-lift.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-loft.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-lump.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-melt.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-mist.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-plot.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-plum.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-sand.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-slip.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-spot.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-step.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-stop.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-trap.webp","A hat was necessary for a child to join the walk.","A pupil without a signed form could take a book.","A signed form was required, but it did not mean a pupil took a book.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","A star was needed for a box to be sent, but not every starred box went.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","After","Agree on a plan before working together. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Agree on a plan before working together. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","All trays other than the green one had two cups.","Anya pulled one handle on a carrying box to check it. When she lifted both handles, the unchecked handle came loose. After repairing it, she tested each handle separately before carrying the box.","Anyone in the show wearing a blue ribbon was a dancer, not a singer.","Apples were in all the baskets; pears were in just one.","Arun crowded the drying rack with wet paintings touching edge to edge. Two pictures stuck together. He moved the next paintings onto separate spaces with gaps between them. They dried without sticking.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Ask walkers which direction they want to go.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Aya packed a painted clay tile while its surface was still wet. The wrapping stuck to the picture. She painted a new tile and left it on the rack until it was dry before wrapping it.","Before","Ben rebuilt the top of his block tower whenever it leaned. It kept leaning because a folded cloth was under one corner of the base. He flattened the cloth and rebuilt the base. The tower stayed upright.","Bo put the brushes away before washing them.","Bo washed only some of the brushes before putting them away.","Bo washed the brushes while they remained in the cupboard.","Both bags held towels.","Both bags were without towels.","Boxes without stars were sent along with starred boxes.","Boxes without stars were the only ones sent.","Changes a printed sound unit or word rather than matching the complete supplied target.","Check player names before announcing a score.","Check soil when deciding how much to water.","Check that string fits before tying a booklet.","Check what is true before acting on a guess. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Check what is true before acting on a guess. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Children could enter whenever they reached the closed gate.","Children entered before the adult opened the gate.","Children wearing hats had to stay at school.","Choose a manageable part and share work that is too much. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Choose a manageable part and share work that is too much. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Choose a word that means the same as begin.","Choose a word that means the same as happy.","Choose a word that means the same as neat.","Choose a word that means the same as quick.","Choose a word that means the same as small.","Choose a word that means the same as strong.","Choose a word that means the same as wet.","Cleaning wet paint quickly can save a model.","Cleo changed the only written plan for her puppet scene and later forgot the earlier ending. Before her next change, she copied the plan onto another sheet. She could compare both endings and choose one.","Compare the initial sounds of recorded familiar words.","D-CONTEXT: The is correctly used at token 1; it is not the homophone error required by this sentence.","D-VOWEL","Dad put out the candles as the last note of the song was ending.","Dad put out the candles before the song ended.","Dan rebuilt a small bridge from a drawing and began putting the drawing away. He looked back at it and noticed a support he had left out. He added that support before trying the bridge.","Dani set out a high stool for the visiting drummer without asking what she needed. The drummer’s feet could not reach her pedal. Dani asked about the drum, then brought a low seat. The drummer could use the pedal.","Dev called out the drum rhythm once and expected the group to remember it. They stopped at different places. He drew a row of beat marks and pointed along them. The group could follow the same rhythm.","Esme stuffed every costume into one small bag. The zipper could not close. She moved some costumes into a second bag. Both bags closed, and the costumes stayed inside on the walk to the hall.","Every basket had both apples and pears.","Every child joined, whether or not they wore a hat.","Every child planted at least three seeds.","Every child planted exactly two seeds.","Every child planted just one seed.","Every child wearing a hat joined the walk.","Every flag was left unpainted.","Every large crate contained books.","Every pupil with a signed form took a book.","Every round and square button was used.","Every round button was used, and every square button was left unused.","Every singer wore the same ribbon as the dancers.","Every starred box was sent to the hall.","Every ticket had been given away before the doors opened.","Every tray had two cups.","Every used button was square.","Explain unfamiliar routines so a newcomer can take part. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Explain unfamiliar routines so a newcomer can take part. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Explain your own mistake so it can be put right. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Explain your own mistake so it can be put right. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Felix tied a large bow across the mouth of his cardboard trumpet. Almost no sound came out. He moved the bow onto the side, leaving the opening clear. He could hear the trumpet again.","Give specific details when another person needs to find something. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Give specific details when another person needs to find something. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Give useful guidance while leaving another person a chance to try. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Give useful guidance while leaving another person a chance to try. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Hana kept adding soap to the wash bowl after the water was already bubbly. Foam spilled over the edge. For the next bowl she added a small amount and stopped when it was enough to wash the tools.","Help repair the damage when something goes wrong. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Help repair the damage when something goes wrong. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Hugo pulled both ends of a knotted ribbon to free it. The knot grew tighter. He loosened one small loop with his fingers instead. The ribbon came free without another hard pull.","Ivy carried a seed packet to the bean bed because its picture looked like beans. The gardener showed her that it was a pea packet. Ivy read the names on the remaining packets before taking the bean seeds.","Jin explained the model while holding its opening toward himself. His partner could not see the part he named. Jin moved around to his partner’s side and turned the model. The opening was now visible to both of them.","Keep drainage holes clear when caring for plants.","Kofi chose a beautiful basket with very wide gaps to carry small counters. Counters fell through. He tried a plain tub with solid sides. The counters stayed inside, so he carried them in the tub.","Lanterns on both tables were lit.","Learning a stitch can help mend a costume.","Leave shared spaces clear for the people who need them. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Leave shared spaces clear for the people who need them. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Lena used a thick brush to paint the tiny windows on her model. Paint covered the wall around each window. She changed to a thin brush and painted the remaining windows without covering the walls.","Leo mixed a batch of plaster before making a space for the mold. While he searched for a clear tray, the mixture became too stiff to pour. For the next batch he set out the mold and tray before mixing.","Look carefully beneath a stopped toy car to find what is blocking its wheels.","Look for evidence before deciding what a problem means. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Look for evidence before deciding what a problem means. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Make every paper fold carefully to avoid tearing a wing on the bird.","Make room for what is needed before adding extras. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Make room for what is needed before adding extras. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Mateo lent out the class puppets without writing down the borrowers. At tidy-up he did not know who still had one. Next time he wrote each name beside a puppet picture and ticked it when the puppet returned.","Max changed the class shop’s opening time on his own note. The helpers arrived at the old time. Before changing it again, he spoke to each helper and changed the shared sign. They arrived together.","Measuring string can help a model fit.","Mei looked for a book by jumping between several shelves. She kept returning to shelves she had already searched. She began at one end and checked each shelf in turn. On the next shelf she found the book.","Mila left her paper shop signs outside when rain began. The words ran down the paper. She made new signs and put them beneath the stall’s clear roof. Rain fell around the stall, but the signs stayed dry.","Music came first, then rabbit feeding, then lunch.","Names a different concrete object from the spoken referent.","Nia was asked to put the seed tray in a bright place. She chose the sunny outdoor wall, where the rain flooded it. She checked with the gardener and moved it to the bright indoor window the gardener had meant.","No dancer wore a blue ribbon.","No lantern on either table was lit.","No pupil with a signed form could take a book.","No tickets remained for sale when the doors opened.","None of the large crates contained books.","Noor finished after Tess but before Sol.","Noor finished after both Tess and Sol.","Noor finished before both Tess and Sol.","Offer backstage jobs to children who prefer them.","One bag held all the towels.","Only one basket contained any fruit.","Only some of the dancers wore blue ribbons.","Only some round buttons were used, and no square buttons were used.","Only the adult could go through the open gate.","Only the green tray had two cups.","Only the lanterns on the left table were lit.","Only the lanterns on the right table were lit.","Only the yellow flag was left unpainted.","Only the yellow flag was painted.","Only two children planted seeds.","Owen filled a whole watering can from an old jug. Water leaked through a crack and soaked the bench. He poured a little water into the next jug first. That jug stayed dry underneath, so he used it.","Pears were in all the baskets; apples were in just one.","Pia copied that the model needed three strips, but left out their length. Her group cut strips too short for the roof. She checked the plan and wrote both the number and the length. The new strips reached across.","Plan how to carry out a job you have promised. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Plan how to carry out a job you have promised. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Rabbit feeding happened after both lunch and music.","Rabbit feeding happened before both lunch and music.","Rabbit feeding happened between lunch and music.","Return shared things to the place where others expect them. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Return shared things to the place where others expect them. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Rosa never watered the pot, even after it dried.","Rosa tried to copy a large map in one hurried drawing. Several streets were missing. She copied one small square of the map at a time, checking each square before moving on. Her new drawing included the streets.","Rosa waited for dry soil before watering.","Rosa waited until long after the soil dried before watering.","Rosa watered while the soil was still wet.","Sam started building the puppet stage before checking its fasteners. He held two walls up for a long time while a friend searched for clips. Next time he collected the clips and walls together before joining the stage.","Share what is available so everyone can take part. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Share what is available so everyone can take part. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Sol finished first and Tess finished last.","Some large crates held books, and no small crate held books.","Some small crates contained books.","Some tickets remained for sale when the doors opened.","Take care of useful supplies that other people share. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Take care of useful supplies that other people share. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","The adult had to open the gate before children entered.","The basket was empty, and both bags were empty too.","The brushes were already washed when Bo put them away.","The candles were out before the song began.","The children stood up and sat down during the last clap.","The first word of a sentence begins with a capital letter.","The green tray had one cup.","The key preserves the passage''s all none relationship.","The last clap came after both movements.","The last clap came before both movements.","The last clap came between standing up and sitting down.","The library opened before the repair.","The library opened while the repair was still happening.","The library stayed closed after the repair was finished.","The players moved between inside and outside all afternoon.","The players remained inside throughout the afternoon.","The players went outside before it began to rain.","The players went outside while the rain continued.","The repair came before the library opened.","The shape of a belongs to another letter.","The shape of f belongs to another letter.","The shape of q belongs to another letter.","The shape of t belongs to another letter.","The shape of v belongs to another letter.","The song had already ended when Dad put out the candles.","The yellow flag was painted along with the other flags.","Theo pulled the ribbons out of a woven mat and forgot their order. Before repairing another section, he drew where each ribbon went. He followed the drawing and put the ribbons back in the same places.","Tickets first went on sale after the doors opened.","Try a small amount of paint on a scrap before painting a whole sign.","Try an unfamiliar role before deciding it is not for you. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Try an unfamiliar role before deciding it is not for you. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Turn a wide object carefully so it can pass through a narrow gap.","Use a complete plan when building a tower.","Use a hand signal when music is too loud.","Use the same conditions when making a fair comparison. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Use the same conditions when making a fair comparison. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Wait for a clear turn when people share an activity. This applies to both different mistakes and their corrections.","Wait for a clear turn when people share an activity. This explains the change from the mistake to its correction.","Writing a complete list can help you remember everything to pack.","Yusuf counted how long two toy cars rolled, but started counting at different moments. His numbers did not compare the full journeys. He rolled them again and began counting at the start line each time.","a bee visits flowers for nectar to take to its hive. pollen sticks to its body during these visits. some pollen reaches another flower when the bee lands there, helping that plant make seeds while the bee collects its food.","a board at our bus stop shows when each bus is due. people use it to decide whether to wait or walk. a roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","a closed gate keeps footballs out of the young plants in our school garden. along the beds, wide paths leave room for visitors to walk and look without stepping on the soil. classes open the gate when their visit begins.","a duck’s soft inner feathers trap warm air near its body. it spreads oil over its outer feathers, which helps water roll off. these different layers protect the duck when it swims in cold water.","a group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. the cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it. for a birthday, ari spent all his coins on wrapping paper and could not buy the card he needed. next time he chose the card first and used the coins left over for wrapping paper.","a model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. the builders moved it onto a side table. at the reading corner, bags covered every seat. rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","a model castle filled the classroom doorway. people bumped it when they entered. the builders moved it onto a side table, and people could walk through without touching it.","a new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. they showed her and practised a slow round. in class, a new pupil stayed standing when a silent signal meant sit down. a partner showed what the signal meant before the next activity.","a toy blocks light from a torch. moving the torch to one side shifts the shadow to the other side. moving the toy closer to the torch makes its shadow larger. the same toy can make different shadows without changing its own shape.","a worker tests the swings and checks the climbing frame before the playground opens. if a part is loose, she puts a barrier around that equipment. she writes the fault on a repair sheet for the repair team.","ada hung the picture list above her own head. the younger children could not see what to collect. she crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it. jin explained the model while holding its opening toward himself. his partner could not see the part he named. jin moved around to his partner’s side and turned the model. the opening was now visible to both of them.","ada hung the picture list above her own head. the younger children could not see what to collect. she crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it.","ada rushed her folds and tore a paper bird. she slowed down at the difficult folds on the next one. malik rushed to announce a game score and read the wrong line. he paused to check the names before announcing the next score.","ada rushed to fold a paper bird and tore a wing. she slowed down at each fold on the next bird, which stayed whole.","adapt","after using the magnifier, sol left it in his coat. the nature group searched the shelf and could not start. sol returned it to its labelled place, where the next group found it.","alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. the paint dried while she searched. before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint. sam started building the puppet stage before checking its fasteners. he held two walls up for a long time while a friend searched for clips. next time he collected the clips and walls together before joining the stage.","alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. the paint dried while she searched. before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint.","amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. its owner came looking for it. amir checked the name inside and returned it. then he checked another blue coat and found his own name. ivy carried a seed packet to the bean bed because its picture looked like beans. the gardener showed her that it was a pea packet. ivy read the names on the remaining packets before taking the bean seeds.","amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. its owner came looking for it. amir checked the name inside and returned it. then he checked another blue coat and found his own name.","ant names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. her friend kept waiting under the tree. asha went back and explained the change. her friend brought his bag to the dry porch. max changed the class shop’s opening time on his own note. the helpers arrived at the old time. before changing it again, he spoke to each helper and changed the shared sign. they arrived together.","asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. her friend kept waiting under the tree. asha went back and explained the change. her friend brought his bag to the dry porch.","at book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading. they put books with missing pages aside. other volunteers ask visitors what they enjoy and help them choose a book to take home.","at the drinking station, a high tap leaves room for a bottle underneath. children can fill their bottles without tipping them sideways. spilled water runs through holes in a tray instead of collecting on the floor.","at the returns desk, a helper scans each book to clear its loan. readers can then borrow something else. the returned books go on labelled trolleys so another helper can take them to the right shelves.","at the sports centre, a timetable shows which room each class uses. families check it before going upstairs. a board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","ava pulled a shared picture book from beneath a pile and tore its cover. she showed the teacher the tear and helped attach a new cover. the book returned to the shelf.","ava tore the cover of a shared book. she helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it. leo knocked over a class plant and broke its pot. he helped move the plant into a spare pot and cleaned up the fallen soil.","bea could not lift a large box, so she carried its loose lids while others carried it. at a display, ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. he made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","bea could not lift the large box and thought she could not help. she carried the loose lids while two others carried the box. the whole set reached the hall together.","bea fetched some paper after drawing a line. she had washed a brush before drawing the line.","bea forgot which seeds she had sown. she labelled the next pots so she could care for each plant correctly.","beans","before choosing a book, noor stacked the cushions. she had stroked the cat before stacking the cushions.","before choosing a pear, lina lifted her basket. she had counted her coins before lifting the basket.","before cooking, our class reads the recipe and measures its ingredients into bowls. this makes it easy to find each amount when needed. after cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","before drying her shoes, tess folded the map. before folding the map, she counted the birds.","before our walking group leaves, the leader counts everyone and checks the list of names. at each crossing she waits until the whole group is together. a helper at the back tells her if someone needs to stop.","before_after","begin — wait does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","behind","bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. the base bent under the model. she tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base. kofi chose a beautiful basket with very wide gaps to carry small counters. counters fell through. he tried a plain tub with solid sides. the counters stayed inside, so he carried them in the tub.","bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. the base bent under the model. she tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base.","beside","bike in front of garage","bo began building before hearing the whole plan. his tower was the wrong shape. he listened to the full plan and rebuilt it correctly.","bo built the wrong shape after hearing only part of a plan. he listened to the full plan before rebuilding. uma guessed where a walker wanted to go and gave wrong directions. she listened to the whole request before answering again.","bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. he put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office. nia was asked to put the seed tray in a bright place. she chose the sunny outdoor wall, where the rain flooded it. she checked with the gardener and moved it to the bright indoor window the gardener had meant.","bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. he put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office.","branch","bread names a separate concrete referent that is absent from the recording.","busy","cause","check","child opens umbrella","child puts cup in sink","child zips coat","children dig hole","children","clock above picture","closing the drawer happened after checking the address. before checking the address, bo had sorted the cards.","closing the tin","cob","cod","cold does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","collecting the menus","compare_initial_sounds","correctedSourceId","costumes hang on rails labelled with each actor’s name. actors find the clothes for their own role there. a repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","counting the tickets happened after tying the bow. before tying the bow, the helper had opened the tin.","dad counted the cups after closing a basket. he had unfolded a blanket before closing the basket.","dad filled his bottle after hanging his coat. he hung his coat after reading his ticket.","den","drawing the moon happened after putting on a coat. before putting on the coat, may had chosen a chair.","dry does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","drying the clay","dug","eli refused an unfamiliar scenery job, then tried moving one panel with a partner and enjoyed it. at music club, may rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. she tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","eli refused to move scenery because he had never done it. at rehearsal he tried moving one light panel with a partner. he liked helping the scene change and chose that job for the play.","eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. he practiced its first short part, then the next part. after joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through. rosa tried to copy a large map in one hurried drawing. several streets were missing. she copied one small square of the map at a time, checking each square before moving on. her new drawing included the streets.","eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. he practiced its first short part, then the next part. after joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through.","ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. a different wheel stuck when he pushed it. he turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again. anya pulled one handle on a carrying box to check it. when she lifted both handles, the unchecked handle came loose. after repairing it, she tested each handle separately before carrying the box.","ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. a different wheel stuck when he pushed it. he turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again.","eve painted a whole sign with thin paint that was hard to read. she tested thicker paint on a scrap before painting a new sign.","eve put out the menus after wiping the table. she had moved the vase before wiping the table.","every_except","eve’s thin paint made a sign hard to read. she tested thicker paint on a scrap before repainting. lou tied all the pages into a booklet, then found the holes too small. he tested the string through one hole before making the next booklet.","fills","finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. the wet joint slid apart. he glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. this time the handle stayed on. aya packed a painted clay tile while its surface was still wet. the wrapping stuck to the picture. she painted a new tile and left it on the rack until it was dry before wrapping it.","finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. the wet joint slid apart. he glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. this time the handle stayed on.","grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. the book was too wide. she asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it. dani set out a high stool for the visiting drummer without asking what she needed. the drummer’s feet could not reach her pedal. dani asked about the drum, then brought a low seat. the drummer could use the pedal.","grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. the book was too wide. she asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it.","grows","had","hana left a tap dripping after filling a bowl. a helper showed her the growing puddle in the sink. hana closed the tap fully, and the dripping stopped.","hana left a tap dripping, then closed it fully when a helper showed her. at the craft table, bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. he took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","helpers rinse empty food tubs before our model workshop. sticky food is removed so the tubs are ready to handle. they sort clean tubs, lids and cardboard into separate trays for the builders to choose from.","hut","imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. the paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. she cut the paper away from the moving wheel. the cart rolled again. felix tied a large bow across the mouth of his cardboard trumpet. almost no sound came out. he moved the bow onto the side, leaving the opening clear. he could hear the trumpet again.","imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. the paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. she cut the paper away from the moving wheel. the cart rolled again.","initial_sound_discrimination","initial_sounds","ivo blamed the wind after scattering the score cards. his friend looked for a loose window until ivo explained the spill. at a match, mae wrote an extra goal for her team. she told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","ivo scattered the score cards and said the wind had done it. his friend began looking for a loose window. ivo explained what had happened, and they put the cards back in order.","jem slid before the child below had moved away, and they nearly bumped. on his next turn he waited for a clear space. at music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. they agreed to play one short turn each.","jem started down the slide before the child below had moved away. they nearly bumped. jem waited for the bottom to clear on his next turn, and both children had room.","jig","jo gave every plant the same water. one pot stayed soggy. she checked its soil and watered it less, and it grew stronger.","jo kept the game scores in her head. after a break she could not remember which team had seven points. on the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. the teams could check the score after the break. mateo lent out the class puppets without writing down the borrowers. at tidy-up he did not know who still had one. next time he wrote each name beside a puppet picture and ticked it when the puppet returned.","jo kept the game scores in her head. after a break she could not remember which team had seven points. on the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. the teams could check the score after the break.","jo tied her shoe after checking the score. she had carried the hoop before checking the score.","jo watered every plant alike until one stayed soggy. she changed its watering to suit the soil. sal gave everyone the same job in a play; a quiet child struggled to announce scenes. sal offered a backstage job that suited the child better.","job","kai switched on the torch after putting down the bag. he had put down the bag after unfolding the blanket.","kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. beads bounced onto the floor. he held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. the beads went into the bottle. lena used a thick brush to paint the tiny windows on her model. paint covered the wall around each window. she changed to a thin brush and painted the remaining windows without covering the walls.","kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. beads bounced onto the floor. he held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. the beads went into the bottle.","keep","kim scattered the board after losing. she helped set it up and asked for another game without changing the result. a runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","kit could not push a wide block through a gap until she turned it sideways. at the pool, ren tried to hear a spoken cue over loud music. he agreed on a hand signal instead, and the group responded together.","kit kept forcing a wide block through a narrow gap. she turned it sideways, and it fitted through.","kit zipped the bag after watching the bird. watching the bird happened after she packed her cup.","labelled tubs separate deliveries for each classroom. a helper puts each parcel into the tub with its room number. another helper compares the parcels with an order list and asks about anything missing.","lamps light the path from the car park to our evening event. visitors can see uneven ground beneath their feet. at the end, bright arrows point back to the car park so people can find their return route.","lap","lea took a ruler from ben’s desk because he was outside. ben returned and could not finish his chart. next time lea asked first, and ben found a spare ruler for her.","lea took ben’s ruler while he was outside, leaving him unable to finish his chart. next time she asked, and he found her a spare. otter used badger’s umbrella without asking. badger searched for it in the rain. later otter asked to borrow it and agreed when to return it.","leaking","leave","leila guessed that drooping leaves meant dry soil. touching the wet soil led her to move the plant from the hot sun instead. arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. a notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. he checked the rack and found his hat.","leila said a plant needed water because its leaves hung down. dad asked her to touch the soil. it was already wet. they moved the pot out of the hot sun instead, and the leaves lifted later.","letter-case:a","letter-case:b","letter-case:c","letter-case:d","letter-case:e","letter-case:f","letter-case:g","letter-case:h","letter-case:i","letter-case:j","letter-case:k","letter-case:l","letter-case:m","letter-case:n","letter-case:o","letter-case:p","letter-case:q","letter-case:r","letter-case:s","letter-case:t","letter-case:u","letter-case:v","letter-case:w","letter-case:x","letter-case:y","letter-case:z","likes","lip","long does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","lp3.cvc_short_vowels.l2.A.short_a.v10","lp3.cvc_short_vowels.l2.A.short_e.v10","lp3.cvc_short_vowels.l2.A.short_o.v10","lp3.cvc_short_vowels.l2.C.short_a.v6","lp3.cvc_short_vowels.l2.C.short_e.v6","lp3.initial_sounds.l1.C.k.v3","lp3.initial_sounds.l1.C.s.v3","lp3.initial_sounds.l2.C.g.v3","lp3.nouns.l1.A.noun_animal.v10","lp3.nouns.l1.A.noun_animal.v4","lp3.nouns.l1.A.noun_person.v10","lp3.nouns.l1.A.noun_person.v101","lp3.nouns.l1.A.noun_person.v4","lp3.nouns.l1.A.noun_place.v4","lp3.nouns.l1.A.noun_thing.v104","lp3.nouns.l1.A.noun_thing.v4","lp3.nouns.l1.B.noun_animal.v102","lp3.nouns.l1.B.noun_animal.v5","lp3.nouns.l1.B.noun_person.v5","lp3.nouns.l1.B.noun_place.v5","lp3.nouns.l1.B.noun_place.v8","lp3.nouns.l1.B.noun_thing.v5","lp3.nouns.l1.B.noun_thing.v8","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_animal.v6","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_animal.v9","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_person.v6","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_person.v9","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_place.v103","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_place.v6","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_place.v9","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_thing.v6","lp3.nouns.l1.C.noun_thing.v9","lp3.rhyming.l1.A.op.v1","lp3.rhyming.l1.B.ot.v2","lp3.rhyming.l1.C.eg.v3","lp3.rhyming.l1.C.ig.v3","lp3.rhyming.l1.C.ot.v3","luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. they spilled whenever he moved it. he divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. he carried both trays without losing beans. esme stuffed every costume into one small bag. the zipper could not close. she moved some costumes into a second bag. both bags closed, and the costumes stayed inside on the walk to the hall.","luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. they spilled whenever he moved it. he divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. he carried both trays without losing beans.","mara nearly recycled a plain bag because she thought it was empty. looking inside revealed the missing puppet shoes. at playtime, ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","mara thought the plain paper bag was empty and nearly recycled it. she looked inside and found the missing puppet shoes. she put the shoes with the puppet before recycling the empty bag.","maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. the puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. she replaced the tray. after the next watering, the shelf stayed dry. ben rebuilt the top of his block tower whenever it leaned. it kept leaning because a folded cloth was under one corner of the base. he flattened the cloth and rebuilt the base. the tower stayed upright.","maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. the puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. she replaced the tray. after the next watering, the shelf stayed dry.","mess","milo kept finishing his sister’s puzzle for her. he began showing one useful move, then handing the pieces back. at music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. he offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","milo took over his sister’s puzzle whenever she paused. she had no chance to try a piece. he showed how to find an edge, then handed the pieces back and waited while she tried.","mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. when the flags dried, the paint cracked. she tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again. owen filled a whole watering can from an old jug. water leaked through a crack and soaked the bench. he poured a little water into the next jug first. that jug stayed dry underneath, so he used it.","mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. when the flags dried, the paint cracked. she tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again.","mira pushed a stopped toy car harder without success. looking underneath revealed a caught stone. leo kept adding water to a drooping plant, but it still wilted. checking its pot revealed a blocked hole; clearing it let water drain.","mira’s toy car stopped. pushing it harder did not help. she looked underneath, removed a caught stone, and the wheels turned.","mock-foundation-word:cut","mock-foundation-word:hand","mock-foundation-word:hug","mock-foundation-word:jump","mock-foundation-word:kite","mock-foundation-word:rain","mock-foundation-word:sun","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.lion","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.monkey","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.tiger","mock.v11.everyday.listening.1.zebra","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.bread","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.broom","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.brush","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.butterfly","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.camera","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.cloud","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.corn","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.dolphin","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.elbow","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.hair","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.hand","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.lamp","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.leg","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.lion","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.monkey","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.penguin","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.phone","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.rain","mock.v11.everyday.vocabulary.1.rice","mock