cs.build.b6.weekdays","mock.v9.phonics.build.b6.weekend","neck","nia guessed a string length and cut it too short. she measured before trying again. bo packed for camp but forgot his cup. next time he checked a list before closing his bag. both avoided repeating their mistakes.","nia guessed the string length and cut it too short. she measured a fresh piece before cutting, and the model fitted.","no","noor drew a map but her friend could not follow it. she asked what was confusing, added clear signs, and her friend found the path.","noor forgot her promised fish-feeding job while playing. the next day she fed the fish before her game and marked the chart. finn promised to bring a banner but left it at home. for the next event he put the finished banner beside his school bag the night before.","noor promised to feed the class fish but joined a game and forgot. the teacher fed them. the next day noor did the feeding job before joining the game and marked it on the chart.","noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. for the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon. leo mixed a batch of plaster before making a space for the mold. while he searched for a clear tray, the mixture became too stiff to pour. for the next batch he set out the mold and tray before mixing.","noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. for the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon.","oi","oli took all the gold stickers, leaving his group none. he returned the sheet and they divided them. at games club, may kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","oli took the whole sheet of gold stickers for his crown. his group had none left. he returned the sheet, and they divided the stickers before finishing everyone’s crowns.","olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. the copied pattern was different. olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. her friend used it to rebuild the pattern. dev called out the drum rhythm once and expected the group to remember it. they stopped at different places. he drew a row of beat marks and pointed along them. the group could follow the same rhythm.","olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. the copied pattern was different. olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. her friend used it to rebuild the pattern.","omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. when the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. for his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead. cleo changed the only written plan for her puppet scene and later forgot the earlier ending. before her next change, she copied the plan onto another sheet. she could compare both endings and choose one.","omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. when the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. for his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead.","only_not_sufficient","opening his bag","opening the atlas","opening the map","opening the register","our class draws the sky and records the temperature each morning. each page has a date. on friday we lay the pages together to find which mornings were warmer and which had rain.","over","packing away the pencils","paying for the pear","planting the seeds","poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. she chose the wrong longer strip. she laid them flat with their left ends together. now she could see which strip reached farther. yusuf counted how long two toy cars rolled, but started counting at different moments. his numbers did not compare the full journeys. he rolled them again and began counting at the start line each time.","poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. she chose the wrong longer strip. she laid them flat with their left ends together. now she could see which strip reached farther.","pup","pupils borrow instruments from the music cupboard. the teacher records each borrower’s name beside an instrument number. when an instrument comes back, a helper checks it and replaces worn strings before it is lent again.","putting away his bottle","putting away the brush","putting away the chair","putting away the hoop","putting on her gloves","putting on his helmet","putting stamps on the cards","putting the book away","quick does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. it soaked through and wrinkled the paper. on the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. the card stayed flat. hana kept adding soap to the wash bowl after the water was already bubbly. foam spilled over the edge. for the next bowl she added a small amount and stopped when it was enough to wash the tools.","quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. it soaked through and wrinkled the paper. on the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. the card stayed flat.","ran","rang","ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. a gust blew two pages across the yard. he moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. the pages stayed where he put them. mila left her paper shop signs outside when rain began. the words ran down the paper. she made new signs and put them beneath the stall’s clear roof. rain fell around the stall, but the signs stayed dry.","ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. a gust blew two pages across the yard. he moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. the pages stayed where he put them.","read_complete_cvc_word","ren closed the atlas after stacking the cards. he had rotated the globe before stacking the cards.","ren could