ebp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/duck-outside-pond.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/eagle-over-mountain.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/hat-on-head.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/kite-over-pond.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/kitten-inside-tent.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/pencils-in-cup.webp","/images/assessment/grammar-scenes/scarf-on-chair.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-classroom/train-on-bridge.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-bend.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-bit.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-cub.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-disk.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-dusk.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-fin.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-flip.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-fog.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-grin.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-hit.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-kit.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-man.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-pet.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-pop.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-rod.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-sip.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-slap.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-slit.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-slug.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-test.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/object-atlas-v1.webp#mock-cell=16","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/object-atlas-v1.webp#mock-cell=18","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/object-atlas-v1.webp#mock-cell=21","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/object-atlas-v1.webp#mock-cell=7","/images/assessment/objective-words/apple.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/boat.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/cap.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/cup.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/deer.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/gift.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/jet.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/mat.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/mug.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/nut.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/orange.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/rug.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/sled.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/web.webp","/images/assessment/release-media/mud-4f3d05c0.webp","/images/assessment/release-media/tub-9c34a66d.webp","/images/assessment/release-media/umbrella-e1f6f2a3.webp","/images/assessment/release-media/vest-9a368716.webp","/images/assessment/release-support/targets/rip-ab8e59.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/at/bat-02.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/bug/bug-02.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/en/ten-02.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/et/wet-02.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/in/pin-02.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/jug/jug-02.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/bin.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/book.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/cot.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/fork.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/red.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/top.webp","/images/child-mode/vocabulary/face.webp","/images/child-mode/vocabulary/trip.webp","/images/prepositions/ball_on_chair.png","/images/prepositions/bird_above_tree.png","/images/prepositions/child_behind_curtain.png","/images/prepositions/cup_next_to_plate.png","/images/prepositions/dog_under_table.png","/images/prepositions/fence_around_garden.png","/images/prepositions/horse_over_gate.png","/images/prepositions/plane_over_town.png","/images/prepositions/rabbit_beside_basket.png","/images/prepositions/rain_through_tent_crack.png","/images/prepositions/shoes_near_door.png","/images/prepositions/slippers_under_bed.png","/images/prepositions/train_through_tunnel.png","/media/initial-sounds/images/p/pencil.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/beach.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/cookie.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/crayon.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/peach.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/pup.webp","A ball rolled into the open doorway. It blocked the door. Mia could not close it.","A bee visits flowers for nectar to take to its hive. Pollen sticks to its body during these visits. Some pollen reaches another flower when the bee lands there, helping that plant make seeds while the bee collects its food.","A board at our bus stop shows when each bus is due. People use it to decide whether to wait or walk. A roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","A closed gate keeps footballs out of the young plants in our school garden. Along the beds, wide paths leave room for visitors to walk and look without stepping on the soil. Classes open the gate when their visit begins.","A duck’s soft inner feathers trap warm air near its body. It spreads oil over its outer feathers, which helps water roll off. These different layers protect the duck when it swims in cold water.","A frog jumped into the pond.","A group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. The cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it. For a birthday, Ari spent all his coins on wrapping paper and could not buy the card he needed. Next time he chose the card first and used the coins left over for wrapping paper.","A little bird sat on my hand.","A model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. The builders moved it onto a side table. At the reading corner, bags covered every seat. Rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","A new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. They showed her and practised a slow round. In class, a new pupil stayed standing when a silent signal meant sit down. A partner showed what the signal meant before the next activity.","A plum is purple. It is little.","A toy blocks light from a torch. Moving the torch to one side shifts the shadow to the other side. Moving the toy closer to the torch makes its shadow larger. The same toy can make different shadows without changing its own shape.","A worker tests the swings and checks the climbing frame before the playground opens. If a part is loose, she puts a barrier around that equipment. She writes the fault on a repair sheet for the repair team.","Ada hung the picture list above her own head. The younger children could not see what to collect. She crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it. Jin explained the model while holding its opening toward himself. His partner could not see the part he named. Jin moved around to his partner’s side and turned the model. The opening was now visible to both of them.","Ada rushed her folds and tore a paper bird. She slowed down at the difficult folds on the next one. Malik rushed to announce a game score and read the wrong line. He paused to check the names before announcing the next score.","Ada rushed to fold a paper bird and tore a wing. She slowed down at each fold on the next bird, which stayed whole.","All the small crates were empty. Some large crates held books.","Alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. The paint dried while she searched. Before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint. Sam started building the puppet stage before checking its fasteners. He held two walls up for a long time while a friend searched for clips. Next time he collected the clips and walls together before joining the stage.","Amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. Its owner came looking for it. Amir checked the name inside and returned it. Then he checked another blue coat and found his own name. Ivy carried a seed packet to the bean bed because its picture looked like beans. The gardener showed her that it was a pea packet. Ivy read the names on the remaining packets before taking the bean seeds.","Asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. Her friend kept waiting under the tree. Asha went back and explained the change. Her friend brought his bag to the dry porch. Max changed the class shop’s opening time on his own note. The helpers arrived at the old time. Before changing it again, he spoke to each helper and changed the shared sign. They arrived together.","At book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading. They put books with missing pages aside. Other volunteers ask visitors what they enjoy and help them choose a book to take home.","At the drinking station, a high tap leaves room for a bottle underneath. Children can fill their bottles without tipping them sideways. Spilled water runs through holes in a tray instead of collecting on the floor.","At the returns desk, a helper scans each book to clear its loan. Readers can then borrow something else. The returned books go on labelled trolleys so another helper can take them to the right shelves.","At the sports centre, a timetable shows which room each class uses. Families check it before going upstairs. A board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","Auntie Meg won a prize for her huge pumpkin.","Ava tore the cover of a shared book. She helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it. Leo knocked over a class plant and broke its pot. He helped move the plant into a spare pot and cleaned up the fallen soil.","Bea could not lift a large box, so she carried its loose lids while others carried it. At a display, Ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. He made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","Bea fetched some paper after drawing a line. She had washed a brush before drawing the line.","Bea forgot which seeds she had sown. She labelled the next pots so she could care for each plant correctly.","Because","Before choosing a book, Noor stacked the cushions. She had stroked the cat before stacking the cushions.","Before choosing a pear, Lina lifted her basket. She had counted her coins before lifting the basket.","Before cooking, our class reads the recipe and measures its ingredients into bowls. This makes it easy to find each amount when needed. After cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","Before drying her shoes, Tess folded the map. Before folding the map, she counted the birds.","Before our walking group leaves, the leader counts everyone and checks the list of names. At each crossing she waits until the whole group is together. A helper at the back tells her if someone needs to stop.","Bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. The base bent under the model. She tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base. Kofi chose a beautiful basket with very wide gaps to carry small counters. Counters fell through. He tried a plain tub with solid sides. The counters stayed inside, so he carried them in the tub.","Bo began building before hearing the whole plan. His tower was the wrong shape. He listened to the full plan and rebuilt it correctly.","Bo built the wrong shape after hearing only part of a plan. He listened to the full plan before rebuilding. Uma guessed where a walker wanted to go and gave wrong directions. She listened to the whole request before answering again.","Bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. He put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. Bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office. Nia was asked to put the seed tray in a bright place. She chose the sunny outdoor wall, where the rain flooded it. She checked with the gardener and moved it to the bright indoor window the gardener had meant.","Bo washed the brushes before putting them away.","Children could enter only after an adult opened the gate.","Closing the drawer happened after checking the address. Before checking the address, Bo had sorted the cards.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “A little bird sat on my hand.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “A mitten fell behind the bench.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “A snail left a silver trail.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “Clouds hid the full moon.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “Do you want some milk?”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “Grandpa fixed my broken kite.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “My sister and I cleaned the cage.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “My socks are in the box.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “One candle lit the room.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “One red fish swam away.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “Our puppy chewed the soft slipper.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “Please shut the door.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “Put your coat on the hook.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “Raindrops tapped against the window.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “The yellow bus turned slowly.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “We can play after lunch.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “We shared the last peach.”.","Compare the sentence start, names, and common words with the capitalization in “Where is my teddy bear?”.","Costumes hang on rails labelled with each actor’s name. Actors find the clothes for their own role there. A repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","Counting the tickets happened after tying the bow. Before tying the bow, the helper had opened the tin.","DRESS","Dad counted the cups after closing a basket. He had unfolded a blanket before closing the basket.","Dad filled his bottle after hanging his coat. He hung his coat after reading his ticket.","Dad put out the candles after the song ended.","Do you want some milk?","Drawing the moon happened after putting on a coat. Before putting on the coat, May had chosen a chair.","Drink the water from the cup.","Each child planted two seeds, and no child planted any more.","Eli refused an unfamiliar scenery job, then tried moving one panel with a partner and enjoyed it. At music club, May rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. She tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","Eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. He practiced its first short part, then the next part. After joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through. Rosa tried to copy a large map in one hurried drawing. Several streets were missing. She copied one small square of the map at a time, checking each square before moving on. Her new drawing included the streets.","Ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. A different wheel stuck when he pushed it. He turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again. Anya pulled one handle on a carrying box to check it. When she lifted both handles, the unchecked handle came loose. After repairing it, she tested each handle separately before carrying the box.","Eve painted a whole sign with thin paint that was hard to read. She tested thicker paint on a scrap before painting a new sign.","Eve put out the menus after wiping the table. She had moved the vase before wiping the table.","Every basket contained apples, but only one basket also contained pears.","Every ticket had been sold before the doors opened.","Every tray except the green one held two cups. The green tray was empty.","Everyone in the show was either a dancer or a singer. Every dancer wore a blue ribbon. No singer wore a blue ribbon.","Eve’s thin paint made a sign hard to read. She tested thicker paint on a scrap before repainting. Lou tied all the pages into a booklet, then found the holes too small. He tested the string through one hole before making the next booklet.","Fill the cup with water.","Finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. The wet joint slid apart. He glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. This time the handle stayed on. Aya packed a painted clay tile while its surface was still wet. The wrapping stuck to the picture. She painted a new tile and left it on the rack until it was dry before wrapping it.","Grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. The book was too wide. She asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it. Dani set out a high stool for the visiting drummer without asking what she needed. The drummer’s feet could not reach her pedal. Dani asked about the drum, then brought a low seat. The drummer could use the pedal.","Hana left a tap dripping, then closed it fully when a helper showed her. At the craft table, Bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. He took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","Helpers rinse empty food tubs before our model workshop. Sticky food is removed so the tubs are ready to handle. They sort clean tubs, lids and cardboard into separate trays for the builders to choose from.","I can bend my elbow.","I can bend my leg.","I can brush my hair.","I can eat some bread.","I can eat some meat.","I can eat some rice.","I can eat some watermelon.","I can hear the rain.","I can hold the brush.","I can open my mouth.","I can open the window.","I can see a cloud.","I can sweep with the broom.","I can take a photo with the camera.","I can talk on the phone.","I can turn on the lamp.","I can wash at the sink.","I can wave my hand.","I can wear my watch.","I have a loose tooth.","I kick the ball hard.","I wash my hands with soap.","Imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. The paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. She cut the paper away from the moving wheel. The cart rolled again. Felix tied a large bow across the mouth of his cardboard trumpet. Almost no sound came out. He moved the bow onto the side, leaving the opening clear. He could hear the trumpet again.","It","Ivo blamed the wind after scattering the score cards. His friend looked for a loose window until Ivo explained the spill. At a match, Mae wrote an extra goal for her team. She told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","Jem slid before the child below had moved away, and they nearly bumped. On his next turn he waited for a clear space. At music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. They agreed to play one short turn each.","Jin fed the rabbit after lunch but before the music lesson.","Jo gave every plant the same water. One pot stayed soggy. She checked its soil and watered it less, and it grew stronger.","Jo kept the game scores in her head. After a break she could not remember which team had seven points. On the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. The teams could check the score after the break. Mateo lent out the class puppets without writing down the borrowers. At tidy-up he did not know who still had one. Next time he wrote each name beside a puppet picture and ticked it when the puppet returned.","Jo tied her shoe after checking the score. She had carried the hoop before checking the score.","Jo watered every plant alike until one stayed soggy. She changed its watering to suit the soil. Sal gave everyone the same job in a play; a quiet child struggled to announce scenes. Sal offered a backstage job that suited the child better.","KIT","Kai switched on the torch after putting down the bag. He had put down the bag after unfolding the blanket.","Kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. Beads bounced onto the floor. He held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. The beads went into the bottle. Lena used a thick brush to paint the tiny windows on her model. Paint covered the wall around each window. She changed to a thin brush and painted the remaining windows without covering the walls.","Kim scattered the board after losing. She helped set it up and asked for another game without changing the result. A runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. Later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","Kit could not push a wide block through a gap until she turned it sideways. At the pool, Ren tried to hear a spoken cue over loud music. He agreed on a hand signal instead, and the group responded together.","Kit kept forcing a wide block through a narrow gap. She turned it sideways, and it fitted through.","Kit zipped the bag after watching the bird. Watching the bird happened after she packed her cup.","LOT","Labelled tubs separate deliveries for each classroom. A helper puts each parcel into the tub with its room number. Another helper compares the parcels with an order list and asks about anything missing.","Lamps light the path from the car park to our evening event. Visitors can see uneven ground beneath their feet. At the end, bright arrows point back to the car park so people can find their return route.","Lea took Ben’s ruler while he was outside, leaving him unable to finish his chart. Next time she asked, and he found her a spare. Otter used Badger’s umbrella without asking. Badger searched for it in the rain. Later Otter asked to borrow it and agreed when to return it.","Leila guessed that drooping leaves meant dry soil. Touching the wet soil led her to move the plant from the hot sun instead. Arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. A notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. He checked the rack and found his hat.","Lena used all the round buttons and none of the square buttons.","Luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. They spilled whenever he moved it. He divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. He carried both trays without losing beans. Esme stuffed every costume into one small bag. The zipper could not close. She moved some costumes into a second bag. Both bags closed, and the costumes stayed inside on the walk to the hall.","Mara nearly recycled a plain bag because she thought it was empty. Looking inside revealed the missing puppet shoes. At playtime, Ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. Ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","Maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. The puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. She replaced the tray. After the next watering, the shelf stayed dry. Ben rebuilt the top of his block tower whenever it leaned. It kept leaning because a folded cloth was under one corner of the base. He flattened the cloth and rebuilt the base. The tower stayed upright.","Mia washed a plate, dried it, and put it on the shelf.","Milo kept finishing his sister’s puzzle for her. He began showing one useful move, then handing the pieces back. At music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. He offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","Mina painted every flag except the yellow flag. She left that flag plain.","Mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. When the flags dried, the paint cracked. She tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again. Owen filled a whole watering can from an old jug. Water leaked through a crack and soaked the bench. He poured a little water into the next jug first. That jug stayed dry underneath, so he used it.","Mira pushed a stopped toy car harder without success. Looking underneath revealed a caught stone. Leo kept adding water to a drooping plant, but it still wilted. Checking its pot revealed a blocked hole; clearing it let water drain.","Mira’s toy car stopped. Pushing it harder did not help. She looked underneath, removed a caught stone, and the wheels turned.","Most town buses are painted red.","My socks are in the box.","N","Neither the red bag nor the blue bag held a towel. Each towel was in the basket.","Nia guessed a string length and cut it too short. She measured before trying again. Bo packed for camp but forgot his cup. Next time he checked a list before closing his bag. Both avoided repeating their mistakes.","Nia guessed the string length and cut it too short. She measured a fresh piece before cutting, and the model fitted.","Noor drew a map but her friend could not follow it. She asked what was confusing, added clear signs, and her friend found the path.","Noor forgot her promised fish-feeding job while playing. The next day she fed the fish before her game and marked the chart. Finn promised to bring a banner but left it at home. For the next event he put the finished banner beside his school bag the night before.","Noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. Then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. For the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon. Leo mixed a batch of plaster before making a space for the mold. While he searched for a clear tray, the mixture became too stiff to pour. For the next batch he set out the mold and tray before mixing.","Oli took all the gold stickers, leaving his group none. He returned the sheet and they divided them. At games club, May kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. Next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","Olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. The copied pattern was different. Olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. Her friend used it to rebuild the pattern. Dev called out the drum rhythm once and expected the group to remember it. They stopped at different places. He drew a row of beat marks and pointed along them. The group could follow the same rhythm.","Omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. When the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. For his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead. Cleo changed the only written plan for her puppet scene and later forgot the earlier ending. Before her next change, she copied the plan onto another sheet. She could compare both endings and choose one.","On sports day, Vic guards his bag of sweets so that nobody else gets a single one.","One leaf came from beside the school gate.","One red fish swam away.","Only boxes with a star were sent to the hall. Some starred boxes stayed behind.","Only children wearing hats could join the walk. Amir wore a hat and joined.","Only pupils who returned a signed form could take a book home. Not all those pupils chose a book.","Open the gate.","Our brushes have wooden handles.","Our class draws the sky and records the temperature each morning. Each page has a date. On Friday we lay the pages together to find which mornings were warmer and which had rain.","Our","Pick up the pencil.","Picture for pig","Plant a new tree.","Please shut the door.","Poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. She chose the wrong longer strip. She laid them flat with their left ends together. Now she could see which strip reached farther. Yusuf counted how long two toy cars rolled, but started counting at different moments. His numbers did not compare the full journeys. He rolled them again and began counting at the start line each time.","Pupils borrow instruments from the music cupboard. The teacher records each borrower’s name beside an instrument number. When an instrument comes back, a helper checks it and replaces worn strings before it is lent again.","Put in a bookmark.","Put on boots.","Put on the hat.","Put the seed in the hole.","Put your coat on the hook.","Quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. It soaked through and wrinkled the paper. On the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. The card stayed flat. Hana kept adding soap to the wash bowl after the water was already bubbly. Foam spilled over the edge. For the next bowl she added a small amount and stopped when it was enough to wash the tools.","R","Ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. A gust blew two pages across the yard. He moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. The pages stayed where he put them. Mila left her paper shop signs outside when rain began. The words ran down the paper. She made new signs and put them beneath the stall’s clear roof. Rain fell around the stall, but the signs stayed dry.","Read the full CVC word against close printed alternatives.","Ren closed the atlas after stacking the cards. He had rotated the globe before stacking the cards.","Ren could not lift a heavy crate alone, so he asked a helper to share its weight. Tess promised to make twenty decorations in one evening but finished only two. For the next event she offered to make two, and the group divided the remaining work.","Ren took every shelf out of a toy cupboard to clean it. Later she could not tell which shelf had fitted each space. Before cleaning the next cupboard, she put matching marks on the shelves and their spaces. They went back easily. Theo pulled the ribbons out of a woven mat and forgot their order. Before repairing another section, he drew where each ribbon went. He followed the drawing and put the ribbons back in the same places.","Roots hold a plant upright and take in water. Some also store food for later growth. These jobs happen below the ground, although their effects reach the stem and leaves.","STRUT","Sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. His cousin arrived on the wrong morning. Sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic. Pia copied that the model needed three strips, but left out their length. Her group cut strips too short for the roof. She checked the plan and wrote both the number and the length. The new strips reached across.","Separately recorded, shuffled response pieces support oral sentence/event organization without modeling the completed answer.","Shut the gate.","Signs above the stairs show which platforms are below. Travellers follow the number printed on their tickets. When a train changes platform, staff at the information desk explain the change and point out the new route.","Small pockets keep pencils away from the books in our backpack. Wide shoulder straps spread the weight while we carry it. A buckle lets us shorten the straps when the bag hangs too low.","Sol left the magnifier in his coat, and the nature group could not find it. He returned it to its labelled shelf. Hana put a game counter in a pencil tin by mistake. The next players lacked a counter until she put it back in the game box.","Sol put his bag on the bench after reading the sign. Reading the sign happened after he tied back his hair.","Suri copied a striped flag and thought it was finished. When she held it beside the original, she noticed a missing white stripe. She added it, then compared the two flags once more. Dan rebuilt a small bridge from a drawing and began putting the drawing away. He looked back at it and noticed a support he had left out. He added that support before trying the bridge.","Tariq kept searching the same three drawers for a missing stamp. He could not remember which ones he had checked. He placed an empty card beside each searched drawer and moved to the next one. He found the stamp in a new drawer. Mei looked for a book by jumping between several shelves. She kept returning to shelves she had already searched. She began at one end and checked each shelf in turn. On the next shelf she found the book.","Tess finished before Noor, and Noor finished before Sol.","Tess hid a paint spill until she worried the model was ruined. She told Gran and they cleaned it. Arun concealed a torn costume because he felt embarrassed. After telling his teacher, he learned a stitch and mended it before the play.","Tess pushed all her seedlings into one corner of the tray. Their leaves overlapped and bent. She moved them farther apart into the empty spaces. The leaves no longer pressed against one another. Arun crowded the drying rack with wet paintings touching edge to edge. Two pictures stuck together. He moved the next paintings onto separate spaces with gaps between them. They dried without sticking.","Tess spilled paint on her model and hid it. When she asked Gran for help, they cleaned it before the paint dried.","The ball is below the shelf.","The ball is under the table.","The balloon is above the child.","The bath is full of water.","The bird flies over the tree.","The book is on the shelf.","The butterfly can fly.","The cat is behind the sofa.","The cat is inside the tent.","The caterpillar is on a leaf.","The child is behind the curtain.","The child stands between two trees.","The class drew the labels after opening the packet. Before opening the packet, they had counted the pots.","The class stood up before the last clap. They sat down after it.","The corn is yellow.","The cup is beside the plate.","The cyclist folded the rag after rolling in the bike. Before rolling in the bike, he had hung up his helmet.","The dog is in front of the house.","The dog was under the table.","The dolphin can jump.","The duck is outside the pond.","The fish is below the boat.","The fish is in the bowl.","The flower is in front of the fence.","The group drank water after colouring the picture. They had crossed the bridge before colouring the picture.","The group found the tape after clipping up the plan. They had measured the card before clipping up the plan.","The hat is on the head.","The kangaroo can hop.","The king wears a gold ring.","The lamp is above the table.","The lamp is beside the bed.","The library remained closed until the worker fixed the door. It opened as soon as the repair was finished.","The lunchbox has separate spaces for fruit and sandwiches. These stop soft food being squashed against the apples. Two clips hold the lid shut when the lunchbox tips inside a school bag.","The office records where and when each lost object was found. A label stays with the object. People looking for something describe it, and the office checks the description against the label before returning it.","The penguin can swim.","The plane flew over the city.","The players stayed inside unless the rain stopped. The rain continued all afternoon.","The pond path was built last spring.","The pot had a picture of a bean on it.","The potter covered the clay after smoothing the bowl. Smoothing the bowl happened after washing her hands.","The printed passage gives the answer “3”.","The puppet plays a fox in our show.","The shape of c belongs to another letter.","The shape of e belongs to another letter.","The shape of k belongs to another letter.","The shape of x belongs to another letter.","The shape of y belongs to another letter.","The shark is in the water.","The shelter was beside our favourite climbing tree.","The snail is on a leaf.","The snake is on a rock.","The snow is cold.","The soup is hot.","The spider has long legs.","The spoken word names rain.","The sun is behind the cloud.","The sun is hot.","The teacher hung up the keys after ringing the buzzer. She had fetched the register before ringing the buzzer.","The tent was a present from our cousins.","The trader wore a green apron.","The train goes through the tunnel.","The uses the capital letter needed here.","The whale is in the sea.","There were two tables of lanterns. No lantern on the left table was lit. All the lanterns on the right table were lit.","They are ground to paste.","This is my chin.","Tom’s “over there” sent a visitor to the wrong door. Naming the blue door beside the stairs helped. Mina sent a message asking for “the thing” from the cupboard. Her partner brought the wrong object until Mina asked for the red measuring jug on the lower shelf.","Two builders pulled a bridge towards different tables and loosened a joint. They chose one place together before carrying it. During a play, two children both began announcing the next scene. They paused, agreed which scenes each would announce and restarted without speaking over each other.","Two runners started from different lines, so their race did not show who was faster. They raced again from one line. Bea measured how much two jugs held by filling them with cupfuls, but she used different-sized cups. She used the same cup for both jugs and counted the cupfuls again.","Uma filled a jug after picking a flower. Before picking the flower, she had taken off her gloves.","Una coloured a blank space that her friend wanted to leave white for snow. Next time she asked and held the paper instead. Dad moved a model to tidy the table, but its maker was still arranging it. On the next visit he asked which part of the table could be cleared.","Until the soil dried, Rosa did not water the pot. She watered it as soon as it was dry.","We brush our teeth.","We can play after lunch.","We make a tower with blocks.","We picked apples from the tree.","We wrap a small gift.","Where is my teddy bear?","Worms make tunnels that let air and water enter soil. They pull dead leaves down and break them into smaller pieces. As worms move and feed, they mix material through the soil where roots grow.","Zara pushed the same puzzle piece harder each time it would not fit. The cardboard began to bend. She stopped pushing, turned the piece, and found the position that matched the gap. Hugo pulled both ends of a knotted ribbon to free it. The knot grew tighter. He loosened one small loop with his fingers instead. The ribbon came free without another hard pull.","___ birds cannot fly.","___ cat sat on the mat.","___ close the lid.","___ hen is in the pen.","___ lunch we rest.","___ ship sails on the sea.","___ went to the park.","___ you find my sock?","a bottle holding a drink","a bridge over water","a button on a toy","a clap made with two hands","a cover for a container","a deep part of a river","a folded blanket used for warmth","a footprint left in sand","a handle for carrying a bottle","a handle for carrying a jar","a hinged lid on a toy","a hole made in a board","a label on the side of a jar","a person watching a game","a picture on an envelope","a player who guards the goal","a pocket sewn onto some trousers","a printed address on an envelope","a ring around a bottle’s base","a shelf for holding blankets","a tear made in cloth","a tree’s fallen leaf","a tree’s leafy branch","a wooden handle on a hammer","always — never","angry does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","at","awake — happy does not express the meaning relationship asked for.","baby","ball between boxes","balloon above child","ban