oduction/en-US/mock-v11/e601ff7cd89bb1db69.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/mock-v11/f4fa3a97943731fdf7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/mock-v11/fed3f81c86300f9f50.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/story_page/moonlight-04a34055ff.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/flip-8dd51da9ec.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/glide-844dd73ef8.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/grin-2d5c23f364.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/hunt-fb24fb3891.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/jig-83272b2cec.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/loft-0963547c09.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/mia-washed-a-plate-dried-it-and-put-it-on-the-shelf-551d51c0f5.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/monkey-6e9456fa43.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/on-sports-day-vic-guards-his-bag-of-sweets-so-that-nobody-else-gets-a-si-df0e7d4925.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/plot-d4b20a780a.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/screen-01e88834d5.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/stove-c310941d7f.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/they-are-ground-to-paste-a457b75303.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/tip-27fdea1a44.mp3","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/og/log-02.webp","5","@antonyms_synonyms:antonym_concrete","@antonyms_synonyms:antonym_picture","@antonyms_synonyms:synonym_concrete","@antonyms_synonyms:synonym_picture","A and a are the capital and lowercase forms of the same letter.","A baby moves a rattle back and forth. Music notes appear by the rattle.","A baby moves on hands and knees.","A ball has just left a child’s raised hand and is traveling away.","A bell rang above a door.","A board at our bus stop shows when each bus is due.","A board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","A boy bends slightly with one hand near his mouth and a broad grin.","A boy covers his nose and mouth with his bent arm. Short lines show a sudden burst.","A boy is in the air with bent knees and both arms raised.","A boy leans back, gripping a stretched rope with both hands.","A boy makes a colourful picture on paper with a pencil.","A boy moves a spoon through the mixture in a bowl.","A boy moves forward with his elbows bent and one foot high behind him.","A boy moves through a pool with his head above the water and an arm out.","A boy presses a ball toward the ground. Lines mark where it springs up.","A boy steers a small wheeled car, holding its steering wheel.","A child adds a coloured block to a tall tower of blocks.","A child at a desk opens his mouth wide with his eyes nearly closed.","A child brings her nose close to a yellow flower.","A child extends one foot toward a ball in the air.","A child faces forward with his legs straight and both feet on the floor.","A child has a winter hat on her head and a coat over her shoulders.","A child holds a watering can with her hand as she moves it through the garden.","A child holds food at her mouth at the lunch table.","A child holds the handlebars with one foot on a bicycle pedal.","A child holds the sides of a ladder with one foot high on a rung.","A child lies under a quilt with closed eyes. It is dark outside.","A child lifts one open hand above her head as a greeting.","A child moves a loaded wagon forward with both hands against it.","A child moves along a path, one foot ahead of the other.","A child presses a small shovel into a patch of earth.","A child puts grains in front of chickens that peck at the food.","A child raises a box with both hands while straightening his knees.","A child reaches both arms overhead beside the bed.","A child reaches toward the floor, folding forward at the waist with feet planted.","A child receives an orange ball with her hands while another child watches.","A child rests on a chair with both feet down.","A child tips a glass to his lips.","A child uses both hands to turn a large ball along the ground.","A closed gate keeps footballs out of the young plants in our school garden.","A dog gave a loud bark when Arun opened the gate. Arun then touched the rough bark covering the tree’s trunk.","A fallen cup lies on its side with a puddle spreading across the table.","A frog now jumps. It lands beside the pond.","A girl brings one side of a flat sheet over to the other side.","A girl cups both hands around her open mouth as if calling across a distance.","A girl cups one hand beside her mouth close to another child’s ear.","A girl follows a page in an open book in her lap.","A girl forms lines of words on a sheet beside a stamped envelope.","A girl holds a microphone. A music note floats beside her open mouth.","A girl holds soapy hands under the running tap.","A girl in ballet clothes points one toe and extends her arms on a stage.","A girl pulls the yellow skin down from a banana.","A girl stands facing forward, her eyes open and the corners of her mouth turned up.","A girl swings a rope over her head and raises her feet over the rope.","A girl tips a bottle and a stream flows into the upright cup she holds.","A group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. The cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it.","A hand brings a knife down onto a carrot, leaving short pieces on the board.","A helper at the back tells her if someone needs to stop.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts. It explains the mistake-to-repair change in both episodes.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts. It explains the mistake-to-repair change.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts. The changed action resolves the problem in this episode.","A little bird sat on my Hand.","A long rope lay on Mr. Lee''s boat. We tied the boat to the post.","A loose arm needs a few stitches.","A mitten fell behind the Bench.","A mitten fell behind the bench.","A model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. The builders moved it onto a side table.","A moth flew past me. It circled the lamp.","A new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. They showed her and practised a slow round.","A new leaf opened yesterday.","A pot","A repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","A roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","A runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. Later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","A seal swam past the boat and dived under the water. Back home, Kit broke the seal around the jar’s lid before opening it.","A seed fell into soft\nsoil. Rain came. Roots grew\ndown. A leaf appeared.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget. It explains the mistake-to-repair change in both episodes.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget. It explains the mistake-to-repair change.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget. The changed action resolves the problem in this episode.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","A snail left a silver Trail.","A snail left a silver trail.","A snail slid along a\nwet leaf. Its brown shell\nshone in the light.","A teacher extends one finger toward a spot on the large world map.","A trader called out prices.","A very tall giraffe bent\ntoward a branch. Its tongue\npulled off the leaves.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation. It explains the mistake-to-repair change in both episodes.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation. It explains the mistake-to-repair change.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation. The changed action resolves the problem in this episode.","A worker tests the swings and checks the climbing frame before the playground opens.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","After cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","After lunch, we planted seeds. Each seed went into soft soil.","After lunch, we visit the garden. We look for ripe peas.","After running, I could feel my heart beating inside my chest. I sat beside a wooden chest with a hinged lid and blankets inside.","After the clouds cleared\nsunlight warmed the sand. We\ntook off our shoes.","After the rain, the ducks swim in the pond. One duck dives for food.","Agree on a plan before working together. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Agree on a plan before working together. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Allow a change to finish before the next step. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","Allow a change to finish before the next step. It explains the mistake-to-repair change in both episodes.","Allow a change to finish before the next step. It explains the mistake-to-repair change.","Allow a change to finish before the next step. The changed action resolves the problem in this episode.","Along the beds, wide paths leave room for visitors to walk and look without stepping on the soil.","An adult slides a tray of cakes into an oven while a child watches.","Another helper compares the parcels with an order list and asks about anything missing.","Arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. A notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. He checked the rack and found his hat.","As we walked, a bell rang above us. We looked up at the tower.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","At a display, Ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. He made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","At a match, Mae wrote an extra goal for her team. She told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","At book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading.","At games club, May kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. Next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","At music club, May rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. She tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","At music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. He offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","At music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. They agreed to play one short turn each.","At nine, Mrs. Moss rings the school bell. The class comes inside.","At playtime, Ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. Ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","At the craft table, Bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. He took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","At the door, please leave your shoes here. The floor is clean.","At the drinking station, a high tap leaves room for a bottle underneath.","At the end, bright arrows point back to the car park so people can find their return route.","At the reading corner, bags covered every seat. Rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","At the returns desk, a helper scans each book to clear its loan.","At the sports centre, a timetable shows which room each class uses.","At","Ava tore the cover of a shared book. She helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it.","B and b are the capital and lowercase forms of the same letter.","B","Barking loudly, the puppy ran through the sprinkler. Cold drops flew from its ears.","Bea could not lift a large box, so she carried its loose lids while others carried it.","Bea measured how much two jugs held by filling them with cupfuls, but she used different-sized cups. She used the same cup for both jugs and counted the cupfuls again.","Bees collect nectar to take to their hive. Bees carry pollen between different flowering plants.","Before bed, I feed my fish. It swims up to the flakes.","Before cooking, our class reads the recipe and measures its ingredients into bowls.","Before our walking group leaves, the leader counts everyone and checks the list of names.","Before the bell rang we\npacked our books. Our bags\nwere ready by the door.","Birds sit in trees. A robin watches from a branch.","C and c are the capital and lowercase forms of the same letter.","C","Can we go outside\nnow? Yes, the rain has\nstopped. Take your boots!","Can you hear that\nsound? Mr. Lee rings\nthe school bell.","Can","Carry the bucket with both hands. Water might spill on the steps.","Check identity instead of relying on a quick resemblance. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","Check identity instead of relying on a quick resemblance. It explains the mistake-to-repair c